# RPMP orchestration

- Read `AGENTS.md` for the layer map and hard invariants.
- Shared skills live in `.agents/skills/`; `.cursor/skills/` contains symlinks plus existing Cursor-only skills.
- Auto-use `orchestrate` only for file-changing work. Read-only questions bypass it.
- For MEDIUM tasks, offer `grill-me` before discovery, especially when an in-scope FR or NFR is TBD.
- Read only the relevant `docs/PRD.md` FR/persona/NFR IDs. Do not paste the full PRD into prompts.
- Load `gateway-backend` or `gateway-frontend` before implementation.
- Docs-first setup is complete. The repo remains documentation-only until a human approves `docs/plans/VERTICAL_SLICE_2026-09-06.md`; do not create `backend/` before that approval.
- Plan approval permits backend Slice 1 only. Do not create `frontend/` until a human selects an unblocked frontend backlog card.
- Code work must cite exactly one backlog ID. One agent session executes one ID, stops, and never auto-picks the next card.
- Do not invent Orchestrator vendor fields in the frontend API contract or UI.
